{"id":"R0261","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Each UAV executes local sensing and decision-making independently with D-S evidence fusion rather than collaborative DNN inference; BDCTA 2026 publisher peer-review policy unverified.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"1 INTRODUCTION","Cognitive radio operates on a closed-loop mechanism","Primary research paper proposing a cognitive radio anti-jamming computing framework (read via built-in PDF reader; shell tools not used)."],["E2","PDF",4,"5.2 Test Environment","we conduct UAV formation flight tests","Evaluated multi-UAV swarm formation architecture described in §4.1 and tested in §5.2."],["E3","PDF",3,"4.1 Distributed Anti-Jamming Architecture for UAV Swarms","local interference sensing, feature extraction and decision-making independently","No collaborative or distributed DNN inference across UAVs; individual UAVs run local processing and fuse spectrum sensing via D-S evidence theory."],["E4","PDF",4,"5.2 Test Environment","test environment that combines simulation and field testing","Provides simulation and UAV formation field evaluation with quantitative performance indicators in §5.3."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","BDCTA 2026, February 06-08, 2026, Harbin, China","Event date Feb 2026 and Codex-supplied Crossref published-online 2026-05-04 (https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3801359.3801401 could not be re-opened live); within eligible window."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 INTRODUCTION","Satellite and aircraft communications form the backbone","Full text confirmed in English on original body pages."],["E7","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","ACM ISBN 979-8-4007-2215-8/2026/02","6-page ACM conference proceedings article; E7 marked U because publisher/proceedings peer-review policy for BDCTA 2026 is not stated in PDF and could not be verified on publisher site."]]}
{"id":"R0266","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"F","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"F","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E1","secondary":["E2","E3","E4"],"reason":"Secondary systematic mapping study of autonomous UAV security literature rather than a primary multi-UAV collaborative inference study.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","conducting a comprehensive Systematic Mapping Study","Secondary literature mapping study of existing primary studies; excluded under E1."],["E2","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","examine 185 primary studies published between April 2017","Reviews prior literature rather than evaluating a proposed multi-UAV architecture."],["E3","PDF",8,"3.1 Objective","our research goal is to map supporting tools","Literature taxonomy and mapping without collaborative DNN inference workload execution."],["E4","PDF",14,"5 Results","we classified the 185 selected primary studies","Secondary classification of reviewed articles rather than evaluation of a proposed inference method."],["E5","PDF",1,"Footer","ACM 1557-7392/2026/10-ART","Journal Just Accepted manuscript dated Oct 2026; Codex-supplied Crossref published-online 2026-10-30 (https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3860892 could not be re-opened live); within window."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","Over the past decade, autonomous aerial systems","Full text confirmed in English on original body pages."],["E7","PDF",1,"Footer","ACM Trans. Softw. Eng. Methodol.","54-page peer-reviewed Just Accepted journal article in ACM TOSEM (though non-primary under E1)."]]}
{"id":"R0269","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Single ground mmWave probe and laptop identify individual target drones; no multi-UAV architecture or collaborative DNN inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 INTRODUCTION","we propose our digital drone forensics system","Primary research article introducing the DroneTrace RF-based drone identification system."],["E2","PDF",11,"6 SYSTEM PROTOTYPE & EVALUATION","The experiments were conducted on 36 drones","Drones are individual passive targets interrogated by a single ground probe; p20 §10 mentions drone swarms only as a future challenge."],["E3","PDF",11,"6 SYSTEM PROTOTYPE & EVALUATION","identification system is implemented on a laptop","Standalone DNN inference runs on a single laptop rather than collaboratively across UAVs."],["E4","PDF",13,"7.1 Drone Identification Accuracy","evaluate the ability of DroneTrace to identify different drones","Empirical lab and field evaluation across 36 commodity drones."],["E5","PDF",1,"Footer","Publication date: June 2022","PDF issue publication date June 2022 and Codex-supplied Crossref published-online 2022-07-07 (https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3534598 could not be re-opened live); wholly within window."],["E6","PDF",2,"1 INTRODUCTION","In past decades, drones have been developed","Full text confirmed in English on original body pages."],["E7","PDF",21,"ACKNOWLEDGMENTS","We thank all and anonymous reviewers","Peer-reviewed 25-page ACM IMWUT journal article with full method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0271","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Evaluated system is a single ground LiDAR and host computer detecting/tracking target drone swarms rather than a multi-UAV collaborative inference architecture.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 INTRODUCTION","investigates the development of a LiDAR-based system, LiSWARM","Primary research paper proposing the LiSWARM detection and tracking pipeline."],["E2","PDF",7,"5.1 Setup","LiDAR hardware connected to a Linux-based compute node","Single ground LiDAR and compute node; drone swarms are the detected targets, not a multi-UAV system architecture."],["E3","PDF",4,"3.2.2 Classification Algorithms","Neural network (NN) models for recognizing the drones","Standalone NN classifier runs on one host computer with CPU-GPU load balancing, not collaborative multi-UAV inference."],["E4","PDF",6,"5.1 Setup","evaluate it at 2 droneshow events","Validated in real-world drone show field tests and large-scale simulation."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","MobiSys '25, June 23-27, 2025, Anaheim, CA, USA","Event date June 2025 and Codex-supplied Crossref published-online 2025-09-25 (https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3711875.3729156 could not be re-opened live); wholly within window."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 INTRODUCTION","Drone swarms have recently exhibited a tremendous growth","Full text confirmed in English on original body pages."],["E7","PDF",12,"ACKNOWLEDGMENTS","thank the shepherd and the anonymous reviewers","Peer-reviewed 15-page full ACM MobiSys '25 conference paper with full method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0272","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Neural network is used strictly as a DRL trajectory and wireless-charging optimizer rather than for collaborative DNN inference workloads.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",3,"1 Introduction","propose a novel two-stage deep reinforcement learning framework","Primary research article proposing an IRS-assisted UAV wireless charging model and SCA-GMAPPO."],["E2","PDF",6,"3.1 System Model","a fleet of UAVs is periodically dispatched","Explicit multi-UAV setting evaluated with multiple UAVs in §5.2.5 and Table 2."],["E3","PDF",14,"4 Solution","determines the future movement path and charging duration","DRL actor-critic network optimizes UAV trajectory and wireless charging only; no collaborative DNN inference workload."],["E4","PDF",19,"5.1 Parameter Setting","All experiments are conducted on a Ubuntu","Simulation evaluation comparing SCA-GMAPPO against four baselines across multiple network parameters."],["E5","PDF",1,"Footer","Publication date: March 2026","Issue date March 2026, accepted 2 January 2026 (p38), and Codex-supplied Crossref published-online 2026-03-10 (https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3789206 could not be re-opened live); within window."],["E6","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","Wireless Rechargeable Sensor Networks (WRSNs) are regarded","Full text confirmed in English on original body pages."],["E7","PDF",38,"History","Received 28 April 2025; revised 16 December 2025; accepted 2 January 2026","Peer-reviewed 38-page ACM TOSN journal article with editorial review history and reviewer acknowledgment on p1."]]}
{"id":"R0281","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"F","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"F","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"F"},"primary":"E1","secondary":["E7","E2","E3","E4"],"reason":"Workshop and challenge organizer overview report rather than a peer-reviewed primary research article on multi-UAV collaborative inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"1 Background and Motivation","UAVM'26 was the fourth edition of the workshop series","Organizer summary of workshop program, PairUAV challenge, and accepted papers; non-primary contribution."],["E2","PDF",2,"3.1 Task and Dataset","given a source image and a target image","Describes single-agent terminal-range pose alignment challenge rather than an evaluated multi-UAV architecture."],["E3","PDF",2,"3.3 Results","puts a light pose head on a frozen","Summarizes external challenge entries for pose estimation; no collaborative multi-UAV DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",2,"3.3 Results","The two leading teams submitted no accompanying paper","Reports challenge leaderboard results from participants rather than evaluating an author-proposed inference method."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","MM '26, November 10-14, 2026, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil","Event date Nov 2026 and Codex-supplied Crossref published-online 2026-11-09 (https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3767308.3842139 could not be re-opened live); within window."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 Background and Motivation","Uncrewed aerial vehicles (UAVs), also known as drones","Full text confirmed in English on original body pages."],["E7","PDF",3,"3.4 Accepted Papers","11 papers were accepted","5-page workshop organizer overview/editorial report lacking primary method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0292","access":"READ","decision":"AWAITING_CLASSIFICATION","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"","secondary":[],"reason":"E1-E6 are met (two-UAV OSTrack tracking handoff with HIL evaluation), but DroNet 2025 organizer website https://sites.google.com/view/dronet2025/home could not be opened to verify the exact workshop peer-review policy and track.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 INTRODUCTION","introduce the vision based handover protocol that leverages","Primary research paper proposing an autonomous multi-UAV marine tracking and handoff system."],["E2","PDF",3,"4 COOPERATIVE CONTINUOUS TRACKING","proposed system comprises two quadrotor UAVs, D1 and D2","Explicit two-UAV architecture with Wi-Fi inter-UAV coordination."],["E3","PDF",4,"4.1 Handoff Protocol","D1 then wirelessly transmits live tracking data to D2","OSTrack transformer visual-tracking inference workload is handed off/migrated from D1 to D2 via target template transfer and feature matching (evaluated in §5.2 p5)."],["E4","PDF",5,"5.2 UAV Data Handover","onboard system tests were performed in a hardware-in-the-loop","Evaluates five deep trackers on a marine dataset, D1-D2 handover matching, and onboard Jetson Nano HIL execution."],["E5","PDF",1,"Footer","MobiSys '25, June 23-27, 2025, Anaheim, CA, USA","Event date June 2025 and Codex-supplied Crossref published-online 2025-09-25 (https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3711875.3737661 could not be re-opened live); wholly within window."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 INTRODUCTION","Effective monitoring of marine animals, such as sharks","Full text confirmed in English on original body pages."],["E7","https://dronet25.hotcrp.com/deadlines",0,"Deadlines","Submissions must be completed by this deadline to be reviewed.","HotCRP shows Program committee and review deadline (and 6 of 6 submissions accepted), but https://sites.google.com/view/dronet2025/home could not be opened to confirm exact DroNet 2025 peer-review policy and track."],["E7","https://researchers.mq.edu.au/en/publications/continuous-marine-monitoring-via-autonomous-uav-handoff/",0,"Research output","Conference proceeding contribution › peer-review","Author-university archive labels peer-review, but institutional repository label alone does not settle official workshop track policy per P03 E7."]]}
{"id":"R0294","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"F","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"F"},"primary":"E7","secondary":["E3","E4"],"reason":"Vision/position workshop paper presenting planned future research without a concrete inference procedure or any experimental, simulation, or analytical evaluation.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"1 INTRODUCTION","The vision of this paper is to amplify","Proposes an architectural vision for adaptive networked UAVs."],["E2","PDF",1,"1 INTRODUCTION","effectively harnessing networks of drones operating in concert","Explicitly identifies a networked multi-UAV architecture throughout §§1-4."],["E3","PDF",3,"3 COLLABORATIVE VISUAL INFERENCE","Our plan is to investigate collaborative visual inference","Only proposes future plans for ensemble visual inference with no implemented or evaluated inference workload."],["E4","PDF",2,"2 ROBUST AERIAL NAVIGATION SANS GPS","We plan to test our system by autonomously navigating","Contains no experiments, simulations, or mathematical performance analysis; all evaluation is stated as future plans."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","Dronet '21, June 24, 2021, Virtual, WI, USA","Event date June 2021 and Codex-supplied Crossref published-online 2021-07-30 (https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3469259.3470488 could not be re-opened live); wholly within window."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 INTRODUCTION","Unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs), or drones, are envisioned","Full text confirmed in English on original body pages."],["E7","PDF",5,"4.2 Leveraging the UAV Mobility for a Self-Healing Aerial Network","Our final task would be to evaluate the performance","6-page workshop vision paper lacking defined inference procedure and evaluation results required by P03 E7."]]}
{"id":"R0298","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Neural networks are used solely as a MARL policy optimizer for UAV moving, sensing, and charging scheduling rather than collaborative DNN inference; publisher peer-review policy not verified.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 INTRODUCTION","we propose MCMU, a novel multi-agent reinforcement learning","Primary research paper proposing a multi-task constrained MARL method for UAV crowd sensing."],["E2","PDF",7,"5.1 Experimental Setups","5 UAVs are randomly initialized in the target area","Explicit multi-UAV setting modeled in §2.1 and evaluated with five UAVs in §5."],["E3","PDF",3,"2.1 System Overview","help them make appropriate moving, sensing, and charging decisions","CNN/MLP actor-critic networks serve only as a MARL scheduling optimizer, not collaborative DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",7,"5.1 Experimental Setups","We construct and train K=20 tasks in our experiments","Evaluated via trace-driven simulation on an NYC incident dataset plus convergence and generalization proofs."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","MOBIHOC '24, October 14-17, 2024, Athens, Greece","Event date Oct 2024 and Codex-supplied ACM DL published date 2024-10-01 (https://doi.org/10.1145/3641512.3686367 could not be re-opened live); wholly within window."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 INTRODUCTION","Nowadays, unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) equipped with specialized sensors","Full text confirmed in English on original body pages."],["E7","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","ACM, New York, NY, USA, 10 pages","10-page MobiHoc '24 conference paper with method and evaluation; E7 marked U because explicit publisher/proceedings peer-review statement was not in PDF or directly opened."]]}
{"id":"R0299","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Single-model optical image detector evaluated offline to detect target UAVs; no multi-UAV architecture or collaborative DNN inference, and publisher peer-review policy unverified.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 INTRODUCTION","introduces a new framework named MAHR-Net","Primary research paper proposing a YOLO-based UAV object detection architecture."],["E2","PDF",5,"4.1 The Evaluation Indicator Comparison","built a uav dataset called UAVD for training","UAVs are detected targets in an offline image dataset; no multi-UAV system architecture is evaluated."],["E3","PDF",5,"4.1 The Evaluation Indicator Comparison","our model, despite being a single model","Standalone single-model CNN detector without distributed or collaborative multi-UAV inference."],["E4","PDF",5,"4.1 The Evaluation Indicator Comparison","compare the proposed network with other state-of-the-art methods","Experimental benchmark evaluation on the UAVD dataset against YOLO baselines."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","ICCMT 2025, June 06-08, 2025, Sanming, China","Event date June 2025 and Codex-supplied Crossref published-online 2025-09-15 (https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3757749.3757787 could not be re-opened live); wholly within window."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 INTRODUCTION","With the advancement of artificial intelligence technology","Full text confirmed in English on original body pages."],["E7","PDF",5,"Acknowledgments","organizers of the conference and the judges","6-page ACM ICCMT 2025 conference paper; E7 marked U because publisher-side peer-review policy was not directly verified."]]}
{"id":"R0302","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Each nano-UAV runs standalone onboard CNN pest detection independently on a separate vineyard partition with no inter-UAV communication or collaborative DNN inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","designing a two-level autonomous transportation system","Primary research article proposing an autonomous nano-UAV and ground-robot pest control system."],["E2","PDF",20,"6 Conclusions","using a swarm of 25 UAVs to explore","Explicit multi-UAV fleet of 25 nano-UAVs modeled and simulated in §4.3."],["E3","PDF",19,"5.2 Routing","does not involve communication between UAVs","Each nano-UAV executes standalone onboard CNN inference independently on its assigned 40x40 m area without inter-UAV collaboration."],["E4","PDF",13,"4.1.2 Embedded system deployment performance","comprehensive evaluation of the performance of all models","Provides onboard GAP9 SoC inference benchmarks plus Webots and multi-UAV vineyard simulations."],["E5","PDF",1,"arXiv stamp","arXiv:2502.14455v1 [cs.RO] 20 Feb 2025","Assessed AAM version dated 2025-02-20; Codex-supplied Crossref published-online for VoR 10.1145/3719210 is 2025-06-30 (neither Crossref nor arXiv URL could be opened via browse); wholly within window."],["E6","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","Heterogeneous ground-aerial autonomous robots combine the advantages","Full text confirmed in English on original body pages."],["E7","PDF",1,"Header","accepted for publication in the 2025 ACM Journal","23-page Author Accepted Manuscript explicitly accepted in peer-reviewed ACM Journal on Autonomous Transportation Systems with full method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0309","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Standalone single-GPU YOLOv8n detector evaluated offline on an aerial dataset; no multi-UAV architecture or collaborative inference, and publisher peer-review policy unverified.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"2 RDC-YOLOv8n algorithm","an improved target detection algorithm RDC-YOLOv8n is proposed","Primary research paper proposing an improved YOLOv8n architecture for small UAV detection."],["E2","PDF",5,"3.1 Experimental dataset","use the MOT_FLY_V0.3 dataset for experimental evaluation","Evaluated offline on a dataset of UAV images rather than on a multi-UAV system architecture."],["E3","PDF",5,"3.2 Experimental environment and parameters","hardware parameters are shown in Table 2","Standalone single-model detector trained and evaluated on one RTX 3060 GPU; no collaborative multi-UAV inference."],["E4","PDF",6,"3.4 Ablation experiment","structures are evaluated by ablation experiments","Provides ablation studies and comparative benchmarks against four detector baselines."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","AIPR 2024, September 20-22, 2024, Xiamen, China","Event date Sept 2024 and Codex-supplied Crossref published-online 2025-06-27 (https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145/3703935.3704093 could not be re-opened live); wholly within window."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 INTRODUCTION","In recent years, drone technology has developed rapidly","Full text confirmed in English on original body pages."],["E7","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","ACM, New York, NY, USA, 8 pages","8-page ACM AIPR 2024 conference paper; E7 marked U because publisher-side peer-review policy was not directly opened."]]}
{"id":"R0317","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Evaluates generic wireless clients for decentralized model training rather than a multi-UAV architecture or collaborative DNN inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"I. INTRODUCTION","propose a new algorithm De-RPOTA for resource-constrained decentralized learning","Primary research journal article introducing the De-RPOTA decentralized learning algorithm."],["E2","PDF",10,"V.A Experimental Setup","In our experiments, we work with 12 clients","Evaluated on generic wireless clients on a cloud server; p1 §I mentions Drone Swarm Cooperation only in passing."],["E3","PDF",10,"V.A Experimental Setup","we train the ResNet-18 model on the MNIST","Decentralized training and over-the-air model parameter aggregation only; no collaborative DNN inference workload."],["E4","PDF",10,"V. EXPERIMENTS","conduct comprehensive experiments to assess the efficacy","Provides theoretical convergence/privacy proofs and empirical training experiments on MNIST and CIFAR-10."],["E5","PDF",1,"Footnote","Date of publication 1 October 2024","Verified directly on physical p1 (issue December 2024, current version 19 December 2024; IEEE Xplore download date 27 Nov 2026 distinguished; DOI URL could not be re-opened live); wholly within window."],["E6","PDF",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","exponential growth in data at the network edge","Full text confirmed in English on original body pages."],["E7","PDF",1,"Footnote","accepted 30 July 2024; approved by IEEE/ACM","Peer-reviewed 13-page IEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking journal article with full editorial history."]]}
